sentences.l:
So then he spoke, and to her wingless was the speech,
and she opened the doors of the well-inhabited halls,
and set out to go;

She found then Odysseus among the slain corpses,
spattered with blood and gore like a lion,
who, having eaten of a field-dwelling ox, goes on his way;

Fifty, I tell you, there are in the halls, women,
maidservants, whom we have taught to work at tasks,
to card wool and to endure slavery;

First then the corpses they carried, those who had died,
and down beneath the portico they set them, of the well-fenced courtyard,
propping them against one another;

But Telemachus and the cowherd and the swineherd
with shovels the floor of the close-built house
scraped;

So then he spoke, and a cable of a dark-prowed ship
from a great pillar having fastened, he threw round the round house,
stretching it high up, so that none with her feet might reach the ground.

But come, to you a cloak and a tunic, garments, let me bring,
and do not thus in rags wrapped, as to your broad shoulders,
stand in the halls;

And they poured themselves around and greeted Odysseus,
and kissed him, gladly welcoming, both head and shoulders
and hands, taking hold of them;
